# Enforce LF line endings for all text files, in the repository and on checkout
# (every platform). The team develops on Linux/macOS; modern Windows editors
# (Rider, Visual Studio, VS Code) handle LF fine. `text=auto` lets git detect
# text vs binary, so binary files are left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must always be LF (they are executed on Linux/COS).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary file types — never apply line-ending conversion (belt-and-suspenders;
# harmless if a type is not present in the repo).
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.psess binary
